From 0c17643f94a4cc2d7641eefd6e33879d3e039b14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unknown <unknown@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:49:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ramips: add support for HiWiFi C312B (R33)

Add support for the HiWiFi C312B, a MT7620A based router with 128 MiB
NAND flash and an external RTL8367RB switch.

The MT7620 NAND controller is supported by a new driver written against
the raw NAND framework.  It keeps the legacy hardware ECC layout (three
parity bytes per 512 byte sector, with single bit errors located and
corrected in software), the vendor OOB layout and the vendor bad block
marker positions, so images written by the vendor bootloader remain
readable.  The driver is carried through target/linux/ramips/files and
is enabled by a small Kconfig and Makefile patch.

The RTL8367B driver gains device tree quirks to skip the family C
initvals and to force family B handling for chips reporting 0x0020.

Signed-off-by: unknown <unknown@localhost>
